{"type":"thinking","text":"Excellent. This is the core answer:\n\n**route-llmgateway-deepseek.patch.yml**:\n- Provider: llmgateway, displayName \"LLM Gateway\", baseURL https://api.llmgateway.io/v1, api openai-completions, apiKeyEnv LLMGATEWAY_API_KEY (lines 5-9)\n- Model id: deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017 (line 14), reasoning efforts off/high/max (lines 16-19)\n- agent-default-model: provider llmgateway, model deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017, reasoningEffort max (lines 20-24)\n\n**route-opencode-go-deepseek.patch.yml**:\n- Provider: opencode-go, displayName \"OpenCode Go\", baseURL https://opencode.ai/zen/go/v1, api openai-completions, apiKeyEnv OPENCODE_API_KEY (lines 5-10)\n- Model id: deepseek-v4.1-flash (line 15), reasoning efforts off/high/max (lines 17-20)\n- agent-default-model: provider opencode-go, model deepseek-v4.1-flash, reasoningEffort max (lines 21-25)\n- Caveat line 2: endpoint unverified until a keyed run proves it.\n\nI should cross-check with fanout-run.cjs line 3006-3009 (model → patch mapping) and DSH route model lists around 2615/2845 — that's useful corroboration and required source diversity. Also check `.dsh/README.md` or docs mentioning these patches. Let me grep for the patch names and route references. Also, the model allowlist at fanout-run line 2944.\n\nFor proper research: 3-5 research actions. Actions so far (read 2 patch files). I can add: grep for patch filenames across repo, read fanout-run.cjs routing lines 2944-3040, and maybe invoke `dsh` route? No, avoid unnecessary. Corroborate the \"reasoningEffort\" semantics with the `.dsh/README.md` or the skill docs (cli-deepseek-harness SKILL.md). Let me grep.\n\nAlso note: I should verify line numbers exactly. I have the read output with line numbers, that's solid.\n\nNow, one thing to consider: are there other \"two dsh route patches\" possibly referring to route patch selection in fanout-run? Yes exactly these two. Good.\n\nNow let's set up phase_init.\n\nFirst, create dirs: iterations, deltas, prompts. Then config JSON, strategy MD, registry JSON. Then invoke gateway for run_initialized. Then read state (loop). Then iteration 1: write iteration file, record gateway, write delta, run reducer, then synthesis. maxIterations=1 so stop reason = maxIterationsReached (iteration_count >= max_iterations at the check before iteration 1? Wait: step_check_convergence runs at the start of each loop, based on iteration_count from state. At loop start iteration_count=0 < max 1, so continue. After iteration 1, loop returns to step_read_state; current_iteration = 2? Let's trace: iteration_count = count of iteration records = 1; max=1; step_check_convergence: iteration_count (1) >= max_iterations (1) → STOP maxIterationsReached. Yes. So reason = maxIterationsReached. In synthesis, `reason` extract says \"Use the latest synthesis/recovery stop reason if present, else frozen default 'converged'\". The latest stop reason is maxIterationsReached. Use that. Good.\n\nConvergence report: stop reason maxIterationsReached, total iterations 1, questions answered... depends on strategy. The strategy template has placeholder questions. The init step says \"Derive 3-5 key questions from the research topic\". I'll craft key questions from the topic:\n\nResearch topic: \"Which endpoint, model id and reasoning effort do the two dsh route patches in .dsh/patches configure? Cite each with its path and line.\"\n\nKey questions:\n1. Which endpoint (base URL and provider) does each of the two dsh route patches configure?\n2. Which model id does each route patch configure?\n3. Which reasoning effort does each route patch pin for default dispatch?\n4. Which patch does a deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017 lineage select, and does that match its recorded executor model? — this is a natural extension and answerable from fanout-run.cjs. But the topic asks only 3 facets. The 4th question adds corroboration and source diversity. Good idea; it's still in scope, since \"the two dsh route patches\" and this lineage's invocation.\n\nMaybe 4 questions:\n1. What endpoint does each of the two dsh route patches configure, by provider and base URL?\n2. What model id does each route patch declare?\n3. What reasoning effort does each route patch pin for the default agent model?\n4. Which of the two route patches selects the deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017 executor, and does the lineage's recorded model match?\n\nAll answered in iteration 1.\n\nThe reducer will parse strategy Section 3 checkboxes. I'll write them exactly. `answeredQuestions` must match exact text for the reducer to tick the boxes (per the prompt contract). I'll include all 4 text strings exactly as in strategy. But careful: strategy section is machine-owned and reducer may rewrite it based on registry. On first run, the initial key questions need to be imported. How does the reducer discover key questions? It reads strategy Section 3 (legacy-import) if registry empty. Then registry becomes canonical. Good.\n\nNow, the iteration narrative must have sections: Focus, Actions Taken, Findings, Questions Answered, Questions Remaining, Next Focus (per prompt pack), plus the persona's required: Focus, Findings, Ruled Out, Dead Ends, Edge Cases, Sources Consulted, Assessment, Reflection, Recommended Next Focus. I'll include both sets (Actions Taken added, Questions Answered/Remaining). Findings numbered one per line, each with [SOURCE: path:line]. The CLI OUTPUT CONTRACT says ## Findings section with one numbered line per finding; findingsCount equals number of findings. I'll aim for 5-6 findings:\n\n1. LLM Gateway patch: llmgateway provider, baseURL https://api.llmgateway.io/v1, api openai-completions, apiKeyEnv LLMGATEWAY_API_KEY (lines 5-9).\n2. LLM Gateway patch: model id deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017 with reasoningEfforts off/high/max (lines 14-19).\n3. LLM Gateway patch: agent-default-model pins provider llmgateway + model deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017 + reasoningEffort max (lines 20-24).\n4. OpenCode Go patch: opencode-go provider, baseURL https://opencode.ai/zen/go/v1, api openai-completions, apiKeyEnv OPENCODE_API_KEY (lines 5-10); file header marks the endpoint unverified until a keyed run (line 2).\n5. OpenCode Go patch: model id deepseek-v4.1-flash and reasoningEfforts off/high/max (lines 15-20); agent-default pins model deepseek-v4.1-flash + reasoningEffort max (lines 21-25).\n6. Route selection: model deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017 → route-llmgateway-deepseek.patch.yml; any other allowed model (deepseek-v4.1-flash) → route-opencode-go-deepseek.patch.yml (fanout-run.cjs:3006-3009); this lineage's invocation-metadata model is deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017, so the LLM Gateway route is active (invocation-metadata.json:1). Hmm, using invocation-metadata.json as a source is fine (it's part of the lineage, and I'm reading it).\n\nFindings 1-6 = 6 findings. findingsCount 6.\n\nAre all fully new? This is the first iteration; all findings are new. newInfoRatio = 1.0. But for a single simple iteration, 1.0 might trigger convergence immediately. That's fine — maxIterations=1 anyway. Honesty: all 6 are fully new to the research packet. So 1.0. The noveltyJustification: \"All 6 findings were newly recorded in this first iteration; none duplicated prior packet evidence.\"\n\nWait — is that too high? The guidance says fully-new=1.0. There's no prior packet evidence in the lineage, so yes 1.0. Max iteration 1 anyway.\n\nNow, delta file: line 1 = canonical iteration record; then one finding row per finding with id/label/iteration/sources. Possibly add a ruled_out row for approaches? We can add one ruled_out record (e.g., \"dsh route resolution via runtime invocation\" not applicable). Not necessary. But the reducer may use ruledOut; empty array is fine. The delta can include an observation? Keep it simple: iteration row + 6 finding rows. Ensure the iteration row's findingsCount = 6 and newInfoRatio = 1.0.\n\nSources: repo-relative paths, e.g. \".dsh/patches/route-llmgateway-deepseek.patch.yml\", \".dsh/patches/route-opencode-go-deepseek.patch.yml\", \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs\". The template says sources are repo-relative file paths or URL. Good. For iteration narrative citations: [SOURCE: .dsh/patches/route-llmgateway-deepseek.patch.yml:9]. The validate.sh SOURCE_T","truncated":true}
