{"type":"tool_result","callId":"chatcmpl-tool-ae535e47b2f0a5ff","status":"completed","result":"./.dsh/README.md:61:  --patch \"$REPO/.dsh/patches/route-llmgateway-deepseek.patch.yml\" \\\n./.dsh/README.md:67:The last stdout line is a `final` event. Exit 0 with `final.reason.kind` set to `completed` means success. Without `LLMGATEWAY_API_KEY` the run exits 1, and the final event carries `MISSING_CREDENTIAL`. To use the OpenCode Go route, swap in `route-opencode-go-deepseek.patch.yml` and set `OPENCODE_API_KEY`.\n./.dsh/README.md:105:  --patch \"$R/route-llmgateway-deepseek.patch.yml\" \\\n./.dsh/SYNC.md:24:| `patches/route-llmgateway-deepseek.patch.yml` | **hand-authored** route patch | none | Yes. `--dump-config` shows the composed `llm-pi-ai` provider and the `agent-default-model` row |\n./.dsh/SYNC.md:25:| `patches/route-opencode-go-deepseek.patch.yml` | **hand-authored** route patch | none | Yes, same check. Its endpoint is unverified until a keyed run proves it |\n./.dsh/SYNC.md:107:  --patch \"$R/route-llmgateway-deepseek.patch.yml\" \\\n./.dsh/SYNC.md:111:Expected result: exit 0, empty stderr, `agent-default-model` naming `llmgateway` and `deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017`, and `mode: DISABLED` under `session-telemetry-otel`. Repeat with `route-opencode-go-deepseek.patch.yml`, which names `opencode-go` and `deepseek-v4.1-flash`. Any stderr line about an unmatched patch target is a failure.\n./specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/002-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/004-dsh-runtime-folder-and-patches/graph-metadata.json:47:      \".dsh/patches/route-llmgateway-deepseek.patch.yml\",\n./specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/002-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/004-dsh-runtime-folder-and-patches/graph-metadata.json:48:      \".dsh/patches/route-opencode-go-deepseek.patch.yml\",\n./specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/002-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/004-dsh-runtime-folder-and-patches/graph-metadata.json:93:        \"name\": \"route-llmgateway-deepseek.patch.yml\",\n./specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/002-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/004-dsh-runtime-folder-and-patches/graph-metadata.json:95:        \"path\": \".dsh/patches/route-llmgateway-deepseek.patch.yml\",\n./specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/002-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/004-dsh-runtime-folder-and-patches/graph-metadata.json:99:        \"name\": \"route-opencode-go-deepseek.patch.yml\",\n./specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/002-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/004-dsh-runtime-folder-and-patches/graph-metadata.json:101:        \"path\": \".dsh/patches/route-opencode-go-deepseek.patch.yml\",\n./specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/002-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/004-dsh-runtime-folder-and-patches/implementation-summary.md:61:You can point a headless dispatch at `.dsh/patches/route-llmgateway-deepseek.patch.yml` or `.dsh/patches/route-opencode-go-deepseek.patch.yml`, add `.dsh/patches/lineage.patch.yml`, and the composed config selects that route's provider and model at reasoning effort `max`. Telemetry is `DISABLED` and `session-log-deepseek`, `goal-round-driver`, `command-goal` and `plan-mode` are off. Each route provider carries `compat.thinkingFormat: deepseek` and `compat.supportsDeveloperRole: false` and declares the levels `off`, `high` and `max` for its one model. `.dsh/SYNC.md` lists every entry in the folder with its mechanism and source and gives the drift check. `.dsh/README.md` is the operator entry point. `.gitignore` line 234 ignores `/.dsh/skills/local-*`.\n./specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/002-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/004-dsh-runtime-folder-and-patches/implementation-summary.md:67:| `.dsh/patches/route-llmgateway-deepseek.patch.yml` | Created | `llm-pi-ai` provider `llmgateway` and `agent-default-model` for `deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017` |\n./specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/002-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/004-dsh-runtime-