{"type":"thinking","text":"`registryFindingCount` = registry.keyFindings.length if array. `findingKeys` for objects uses id/title/summary/text etc. The registry keyFindings entries have `id`, `text`, sources. The closeout's `countOnlyFindings` sums findingsCount for iteration records without structured arrays. If I include structured `keyFindings` in the iteration record (state log + delta iteration row), then countOnlyFindingCount = 0 for that record. And `identifiableFindingGroups` = record.keyFindings → findingKeys; registry keyFindings keys include id and text; matching by id or text? Since IDs must match exactly. If I make the IDs in the record equal to `finding-1-1-<slugify(text)>`? Ugh, the reducer generates IDs from `finding-${iteration.run}-${index+1}-${slugify(finding)}`. I can't know slugify easily? I can derive it: slugify likely lowercases, replaces non-alnum with hyphen. But matching by text is easier: findingKeys includes `text` for both record and registry; the registry entry's text = finding text; record's `keyFindings[].text` = same text. normalizeFindingKey probably lowercases/trims. So identical text matches.\n\nAlternatively, include `findings` as an array of strings in the iteration record — then countOnlyFindings skips (structured present), collectIterationFindingGroups uses `findings` (research fields ['keyFindings','findings']) and findingKeys(string) = normalized text. Registry keyFindings text matches. That's simple. The record schema is legacy upcast; unknown fields `findings` are ignored by upcast data, but the state log projection might preserve the original row (with findings) or only canonical fields? Let me check what the projection writes. The prompt template says the projection writes the row back. The reducer reads the state log. If the projection drops unknown fields, then `findings`/`keyFindings` won't be in the state log and closeout sees count-only. Hmm. Also the delta file's iteration row can include them; closeout reads `lineageStateLogs(args.artifactDir, mode)` first — if no lineages subdir, it uses the passed stateLog. It does NOT read delta files. So only the state log projection matters.\n\nWhat does the projection write? Let me read mode-append-gateway projection code, or check a previous lineage's state log in the repo (there are other fanout lineage runs from prior packets!). Let me find lineage state logs in specs and inspect a record to see the projection shape. That's the fastest way."}
