{"type":"thinking","text":"Good. phase_init complete.\n\nNow iteration 1. I have already executed the research actions:\n1. Read route-llmgateway patch (exact lines).\n2. Read route-opencode-go patch (exact lines).\n3. Read fanout-run.cjs route selection (lines 3006-3009).\n4. Grep corroboration in .dsh/SYNC.md and .dsh/README.md (read spans).\nThat's 4 research actions (within budget).\n\nNow write the iteration narrative. Structure per prompt pack: Focus, Actions Taken, Findings, Questions Answered, Questions Remaining, Next Focus. Plus persona sections: Ruled Out, Dead Ends, Edge Cases, Sources Consulted, Assessment, Reflection, Recommended Next Focus.\n\nI need to be careful about the parse:\n- Heading pattern: `# Iteration 1: ...` (headingMatch).\n- extractSection(markdown, 'Findings') — likely regex `## Findings` to next `##`. Numbered list item per finding.\n- `## Ruled Out` and `## Dead Ends`; list items → ruledOutDirections. If I include a \"nothing ruled out\" text as a list item, it'd pollute the registry. Keep those sections with plain prose \"[None ...]\" not list items? `extractListItems` filters lines starting with -/*/digit. If I write \"None...\" plain, it's ignored. Good.\n- `## Questions Answered` — not parsed by reducer for resolution (only answeredQuestions record). Still include for the contract.\n- `## Sources Consulted` — extractListItems; each source as `- ...`. Coverage by sources will count entries. Good.\n- `## Assessment` — not parsed except maybe.\n- `## Reflection` with exact labels `- What worked and why: ...`, `- What did not work and why: ...`, `- What I would do differently: ...`.\n- `## Recommended Next Focus` — parsed as nextFocus.\n\nFindings: 6 numbered items. Each with [SOURCE: ...] citations. Note the reducer's `extractListItems` removes the leading number and normalizes; the `[SOURCE: ...]` markers remain in the finding text. That's expected by the template.\n\nLet me decide the exact 6 findings and sources:\n\n1. `1. The LLM Gateway route patch configures provider llmgateway with baseURL https://api.llmgateway.io/v1, api openai-completions, apiKeyEnv LLMGATEWAY_API_KEY, displayName LLM Gateway, and compat thinkingFormat deepseek / supportsDeveloperRole false. [SOURCE: .dsh/patches/route-llmgateway-deepseek.patch.yml:9]`\n   - Actually line 9 is baseURL. Include multiple markers: `:5` provider, `:9` baseURL, `:7` apiKeyEnv, `:11` thinkingFormat. The citation rule says every finding cites a source; multiple citations fine.\n2. `2. The LLM Gateway route patch declares model id deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017 (name DeepSeek V4.1 Flash) with reasoningEfforts off (empty), high, and max, and pins the default agent model to provider llmgateway, model deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017, reasoningEffort max. [SOURCE: .dsh/patches/route-llmgateway-deepseek.patch.yml:14] [SOURCE: .dsh/patches/route-llmgateway-deepseek.patch.yml:16] [SOURCE: .dsh/patches/route-llmgateway-deepseek.patch.yml:24]`\n3. `3. The OpenCode Go route patch configures provider opencode-go with baseURL https://opencode.ai/zen/go/v1, api openai-completions, apiKeyEnv OPENCODE_API_KEY, displayName OpenCode Go, and the same compat block; its header records that the endpoint is unverified until a keyed run proves it. [SOURCE: .dsh/patches/route-opencode-go-deepseek.patch.yml:10] [SOURCE: .dsh/patches/route-opencode-go-deepseek.patch.yml:2]`\n4. `4. The OpenCode Go route patch declares model id deepseek-v4.1-flash (name DeepSeek V4.1 Flash) with reasoningEfforts off (empty), high, and max, and pins the default agent model to provider opencode-go, model deepseek-v4.1-flash, reasoningEffort max. [SOURCE: .dsh/patches/route-opencode-go-deepseek.patch.yml:15] [SOURCE: .dsh/patches/route-opencode-go-deepseek.patch.yml:17] [SOURCE: .dsh/patches/route-opencode-go-deepseek.patch.yml:25]`\n5. `5. Route selection: the harness dispatcher chooses route-llmgateway-deepseek.patch.yml when the lineage model is deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017 and route-opencode-go-deepseek.patch.yml otherwise; this lineage's invocation metadata records model deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017 at reasoningEffort max, so the LLM Gateway patch is the active route here. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:3006] [SOURCE: specs/.../invocation-metadata.json:1]`\n   - Wait, the invocation-metadata.json is inside the lineage; the source path should be the lineage-relative or repo-relative? It says repo-relative file path. I'll use the full repo-relative path `specs/.../lineages/dsh-rc3/invocation-metadata.json:1`. Valid.\n6. `6. Independent documentation corroborates the configured defaults: .dsh/SYNC.md expects agent-default-model naming llmgateway + deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017 for the LLM Gateway route and opencode-go + deepseek-v4.1-flash for the OpenCode Go route, and .dsh/README.md names LLMGATEWAY_API_KEY / OPENCODE_API_KEY as the route credential switch. [SOURCE: .dsh/SYNC.md:111] [SOURCE: .dsh/README.md:67]`\n\nAll 6 fully new except #6 corroboration (partially new). Ratio: 5 + 0.5 = 5.5/6 = 0.9167 → 0.92.\n\nHmm wait: finding 5's invocation metadata: the line is 1 (single line). Fine. Also, do I want to cite `fanout-run.cjs:3015` where routePatch is passed to `--patch`? That's nice corroboration: `args = ['--profile','headless','--patch', routePatch, ...]`. Use `:3015`. And reasoningEffort pin at line 3048. Maybe cite 3006 and 3048. Good.\n\nNow \"Actions Taken\": list the 4 reads/greps. \"Questions Answered\": the exact 4 question texts. \"Questions Remaining\": none. \n\nEdge Cases:\n- Ambiguous input: none; \"two dsh route patches\" resolved to the two files under `.dsh/patches/` that name `deepseek` in their filename and that fanout-run maps to (route-llmgateway... and route-opencode-go...).\n- Contradictory evidence: prior packet `tasks.md:46` cites opencode-go baseURL line 9 and model lines 14/23, but the current file has baseURL line 10 and model lines 15/24; current checked-in file wins; provider/model claims agree,